# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEGIN not-published-by-the-availability-statement
# test_internal_working_documents_are_untracked finds this block by the
# marker line above, so the prose below is free to be rewritten.
#
# Everything the data-availability statement does not commit to publishing.
# That statement promises the analysis code and the processed outputs behind
# every table and figure; a file tracked here that is neither is published as a
# side effect. Working documents stay under _internal/, and reproduce.sh
# regenerates the verification report that verify_claim.py writes.
#
# A pattern here is inert on a path that was already tracked when the pattern was
# written, so adding a line does not untrack anything: every file this block
# names must also be `git rm --cached`-ed once, or the rule reads as enforced
# while the file keeps publishing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_internal/*
reports/verification_report.md
